"message": "Guidelines list chronic kidney disease and Fanconi syndrome as TDF toxicities, with creatinine toxicity grading based on eGFR decline from baseline. Patient's creatinine rose from 0.8 to 1.1 mg/dL and eGFR fell from baseline to 78 mL/min/1.73m² after 10 weeks on TDF. This represents a >10% eGFR decline from baseline, meeting at least Grade 1 toxicity criteria. TDF is the likely contributor given the temporal relationship. Against drug attribution: pregnancy itself increases creatinine clearance demands, and 78 mL/min may partly reflect normal pregnancy-related physiology. Urinalysis is normal (no proteinuria, no glycosuria), and phosphate is normal, arguing against overt Fanconi syndrome. DTG can also affect tubular secretion but less commonly.",
"recommended_action": "Continue TDF with close renal monitoring. Repeat creatinine/eGFR within 4 weeks. If progressive decline or proteinuria develops, consider switching to TAF-based regimen per guidelines.",
